-Held this round (no finding): the remembered claim under two worktrees (each has its own `.cache`, since `./zn` runs from its checkout's root), a claim given back from another worktree and then re-claimed (a new random stamp, so the stale file never matches), a stale file left by z-design's carried `status <id> prepared` (no later origin status carries its value), recombine and fold racing each other over an orphan (the second publish is refused on `preparing`), and id reuse after a retirement (`z-nile/next` is monotonic).
