+### 3. The prompt of a model step (`dispatch.prompt`)
+Seven lines, no pasted text: "You are running the z-nile step <step> for <id>, headless and unattended, under ./zn dispatch."; "Read `<skill>/SKILL.md` and follow it for <id>." (z-ticket: "…to capture this as one issue in the <project> project: "<words>"."; z-run: "…its input is the raft's prompt, `<prompt.md path>`; read the whole file first."; zz-review: "…act as the clean adversarial reviewer of <id> in <mode> mode. Write only the review file that mode names."); "Before you start, run `./zn lessons --when <design|build> --full` and ask each lesson's check of your work."; the worktree; the questions.md path and rule; "Never merge a pull request and never push to main yourself…"; "Record your own spend as the skill says, without --tokens for this session…". Every CLI reads the files itself (claude resolves `.claude/skills`; grok and agent find nothing by name, c0115 E1, so the path is the only reliable pointer: programme review F11).
+
+The raft's `prompt.md` (`renderPrompt`, `z-nile/templates/prompt.md`) changes the same way: the Skills section lists `` - `<path>` `` per skill (c0115's order and project rules unchanged), the Architecture section says "Read `<root>/architecture.md` before you write code: it is binding." (or c0120's "has none" line), and the Lessons section names `./zn lessons --when build --full --skill <each z-nile skill and the raft's project's>` above c0111's index, which stays (Guess G9). The work items, their `check.sh` and their acceptance specs are still inlined: they are the raft's own contract, not "other issues".
